  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Let&nbsp; the circle be</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>x</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>&#160;</mo></mrow></msup><mo>+</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>+</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>g</mi><mi>x</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>+</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>f</mi><mi>y</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>+</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>0</mn></math></p><p>According to the question,&nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>g</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mi>g</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mi>i</mi></mfenced></math>&nbsp;</p><p>and&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</p><p><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><msqrt><msup><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mi>c</mi></msqrt><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn><msqrt><mn>7</mn></msqrt><mo>&#8658;</mo><msup><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>7</mn><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mo>.</mo><mfenced><mrow><mi>i</mi><mi>i</mi></mrow></mfenced></math></p><p>The circle passes through the point&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mrow><mn>3</mn><mo>,</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></mfenced></math>, then&nbsp;<br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>9</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>+</mo><mn>6</mn><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>g</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo></math>&nbsp;by&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mfenced><mi>i</mi></mfenced></math><br /><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#8658;</mo><mo>(</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>3</mn><msup><mo>)</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>g</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>-</mo><mn>3</mn></math><br /><math> <mrow> <mo>&#8756;</mo> </mrow> </math><math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mo>&#160;</mo><mi>c</mi><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>9</mn></math>&nbsp;and&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>f</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>=</mo><mo>&#160;</mo><mn>16</mn><mo>&#160;</mo><mo>&#8658;</mo><mi>f</mi><mo>=</mo><mo>&#177;</mo><mn>4</mn></math>&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</p><p>So the required circles are</p><p>&nbsp;<math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><msup><mi>x</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>+</mo><msup><mi>y</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo>-</mo><mn>6</mn><mi>x</mi><mo>&#177;</mo><mn>8</mn><mi>y</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>9</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></math>.</p>"
  }
